# Architecture: masterfabric-go is mandatory

The backend **is** `masterfabric-go` (clean/hexagonal: Chi, pgx, Redis, goose).
Do **not** build a custom backend or framework. All LumiCity features live in the
`lighting` bounded context and must mirror the existing layering.

## Add a feature by mirroring an existing slice (e.g. `tenant`)

```
internal/domain/lighting/        # entities + repository interfaces (NO deps)
internal/application/lighting/   # use cases + DTOs (orchestration only)
internal/infrastructure/postgres/lighting/  # pgx repository implementations
internal/infrastructure/http/handler/lighting/  # Chi handlers
internal/infrastructure/postgres/migrations/    # goose migrations
```

## Rules

- Domain layer imports nothing from infrastructure/application.
- Use cases depend on repository **interfaces**, never concrete pgx types.
- Register routes in `internal/infrastructure/http/router/router.go`; wire
  dependencies in `cmd/server/main.go`.
- New tables: add a goose migration **and** keep `EnsureSchema` (startup DDL) in
  sync so cloud deploys work without a manual migrate step.
- Reuse `internal/shared` helpers (`response`, `pagination`, `validator`, `errors`).
